{"id":136,"date":"2024-12-18T16:29:18","date_gmt":"2024-12-18T16:29:18","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=136"},"modified":"2025-04-10T07:33:33","modified_gmt":"2025-04-10T12:33:33","slug":"forbidden-visions-and-nightmare-quests","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/forbidden-visions-and-nightmare-quests\/","title":{"rendered":"Forbidden Visions and Nightmare Quests"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>If you\u2019ve been following social media, you\u2019ll have seen some pretty big news today from Aconyte Books as part of our Arkham Nights celebration. In case you missed it, here\u2019s a round-up, along with more information on these fantastic upcoming titles. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:15px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-forbidden-visions-of-lucius-galloway-drowned-city-book-1\">The Forbidden Visions of Lucius Galloway (Drowned City, Book 1)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Announced last month, today we can reveal the cover for the forthcoming <em>Arkham Horror novel, The Forbidden Visions of Lucius Galloway<\/em> by Carrie Harris with cover art by Mart\u00edn M. Barbudo.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"588\" height=\"1024\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-588x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-138\" srcset=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-588x1024.webp 588w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-172x300.webp 172w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-768x1338.webp 768w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-882x1536.webp 882w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway-1175x2048.webp 1175w, https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2024\/12\/ark_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway.webp 1254w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 588px) 100vw, 588px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The novel serves as a prequel to the upcoming <em>Arkham Horror: The Card Game expansion, The Drowned City<\/em>, and introduces Lucius Galloway, one of the Investigators featured in the new expansion. What\u2019s more, you can hear author Carrie Harris reading the book\u2019s prologue in the video below, and you can also <a href=\"https:\/\/images-cdn.fantasyflightgames.com\/filer_public\/4c\/5c\/4c5c13a2-3f77-49b1-bea8-1064e5f6e439\/ark_the_forbidden_visions_of_lucius_galloway_-_sample_chapters.pdf?_gl=1*9bahhu*_gcl_au*Njc4OTA3MjQyLjE3MzM5MzY3NzU.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">read the first three chapters online now<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube-nocookie.com\/embed\/elVgf_IDTwo?feature=oembed\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen class=\"w-full h-full\"><\/iframe><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The Forbidden Visions of Lucius Galloway will be published November 19. For more about the book, including pre-order info, <a href=\"https:\/\/aconytebooks.com\/shop\/the-forbidden-visions-of-lucius-galloway-by-carrie-harris\">visit Aconyte\u2019s website<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube-nocookie.com\/embed\/Jr80FdgOTkY?feature=oembed\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen class=\"w-full h-full\"><\/iframe><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-nightmare-quest-of-april-may-drowned-city-book-2\">The Nightmare Quest of April May (Drowned City, Book 2)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>In some of today\u2019s other big news, we can announce that <em>The Forbidden Visions of Lucius Galloway<\/em> is just the first part of a loose trilogy of novels ushering in the Drowned City, and the second \u2013 <em>The Nightmare Quest of April May<\/em> by Rosemary Jones \u2013 is coming Spring 2025!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube-nocookie.com\/embed\/feWiob_vGVY?feature=oembed\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen class=\"w-full h-full\"><\/iframe><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For more information on this upcoming title, and to make sure you don\u2019t miss any news \u2013 including the cover reveal and release date for <em>The Nightmare Quest of April May<\/em> \u2013 make sure you sign up for the Aconyte newsletter.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-tides-of-innsmouth-investigators-gamebooks-2\">The Tides of Innsmouth (Investigators Gamebooks #2)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Earlier this year, Aconyte Books released <em><a href=\"https:\/\/aconytebooks.com\/shop\/darkness-over-arkham-by-jonthan-green\/\">The Darkness Over Arkham<\/a><\/em>, the very first Arkham Horror Investigators Gamebook. Today, we\u2019re pleased to announce the second book in the series is coming Spring 2025.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube-nocookie.com\/embed\/zQbQzXNZKKE?feature=oembed\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen class=\"w-full h-full\"><\/iframe><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>This second volume in the series is fully compatible with <em>The Darkness Over Arkham<\/em>, so if you\u2019ve already completed that adventure and you want to play through <em>The Tides of Innsmouth<\/em> using your chosen Investigator from the first book, you can.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>The Tides of Innsmouth<\/em> will be available for pre-order very soon \u2013 follow Aconyte on social media and sign up for the newsletter to make sure you hear first.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-the-arkham-advertiser-show-giveaway\">The Arkham Advertiser Show Giveaway<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\"><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/www.youtube-nocookie.com\/embed\/eP452-0_OxU?feature=oembed\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen class=\"w-full h-full\"><\/iframe><\/div><\/div>\n<\/div><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you were lucky enough to be at Gen Con this year, hopefully you managed to pick up a copy of the <em>Arkham Advertiser<\/em>, a real, printed edition of Arkham\u2019s esteemed paper of record. The Gen Con edition\u2019s front page featured \u201cGrave Rumors\u201d of some strange goings on in Arkham and serves as something of a narrative introduction to EDGE\u2019s <em>The Hungering Abyss<\/em> roleplaying game starter set \u2013 in fact, you can even use it as an in-game prop to immerse your group deeper into the world of Arkham. If you missed it, you can <a href=\"https:\/\/www.edge-studio.net\/grave-rumors-and-more\/\">download a digital copy from EDGE\u2019s website<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Well, today, we can announce that Aconyte and EDGE have teamed up for another show giveaway edition of the <em>Arkham Advertiser<\/em>, which you\u2019ll be able to pick up from PAX Unplugged in Philadelphia (from December 6-8), and Dragonmeet in London (November 30). Don\u2019t worry, though \u2013 if you aren\u2019t able to make it to either of these events, this new edition of the <em>Arkham Advertiser<\/em> will be available to download from EDGE\u2019s site after the shows. You\u2019ll just have to provide your own smell of fresh newsprint.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>To stay up-to-date with all the latest news on these and other exciting upcoming titles, <a href=\"https:\/\/aconytebooks.com\/aconyte-mailing-list\/\">sign up for the Aconyte newsletter<\/a> and follow Aconyte on <a href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/aconytebooks\/\">Facebook<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/aconytebooks\/\">Instagram<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.tiktok.com\/@aconytebooks\">TikTok<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/x.com\/AconyteBooks\">X (formerly Twitter)<\/a> and <a href=\"https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/aconytebooks.bsky.social\">BlueSky<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":754,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false},"key-tag":[34,17,32],"class_list":["post-136","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-aconyte","key-tag-books","key-tag-novels"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v22.3 (Yoast SEO v22.9) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Forbidden Visions and Nightmare Quests | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News<\/title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/forbidden-visions-and-nightmare-quests\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Forbidden Visions and Nightmare Quests | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"If you\u2019ve been following social media, you\u2019ll have seen some pretty big news today from Aconyte Books as part of our Arkham Nights celebration. In case you missed it, here\u2019s a round-up, along with more information on these fantastic upcoming titles. The Forbidden Visions